Protothread is header-only. There is nothing to build and nothing to link
against: copy protothread.h (and protothread_sem.h and protothread_lock.h if
you want semaphores or reader-writer locks) into your project and include
them. Requires gcc or clang.

To build and run the test suite, and optionally install the headers system
wide, you need CMake 3.10 or later:

cmake -S . -B build
cmake --build build
./build/pttest
sudo cmake --install build

See the "Configuration" and "Bare-metal and embedded use" sections of
README.md for the compile-time options, including how to use protothreads
with no C library at all.
